  "dosing": false,
  "formula": "GCS-Pupils Score = [GCS Score](nabda:calc.glasgow-coma-scale-score-gcs) - Pupil response,\n\nwhere GCS Score = Eye response + Verbal response + Motor response\n\nand other variables are as follows:\n\n| Variable | Points | |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Eye response | Eyes open spontaneously | 4 |\n| Eye opening to verbal command | 3 | |\n| Eye opening to pain | 2 | |\n| No eye opening | 1 | |\n| Not assessable (trauma, edema, etc.) | 1 | |\n| Verbal response | Oriented | 5 |\n| Confused | 4 | |\n| Inappropriate words | 3 | |\n| Incomprehensible sounds | 2 | |\n| No verbal response | 1 | |\n| Intubated | 1 | |\n| Motor response | Obeys commands | 6 |\n| Localizes pain | 5 | |\n| Withdrawal from pain | 4 | |\n| Flexion to pain | 3 | |\n| Extension to pain | 2 | |\n| No motor response | 1 | |\n| Pupil response | Both pupils unreactive to light | 2 |\n| One pupil unreactive to light | 1 | |\n| Both pupils reactive to light (normal) | 0 | |",
  "how_to_use": {
    "why": "",
    "when": "Patients atteints de traumatisme crânien.",
    "pearls": "- Score dérivé rétrospectivement, à partir de données poolées issues de deux grandes bases de données, IMPACT et CRASH.\n- L'ajout des données pupillaires s'est révélé particulièrement utile aux scores GCS très bas (3-4), probablement en raison d'une fréquence plus élevée de réponse pupillaire anormale chez les patients présentant un traumatisme crânien grave (TBI) et un GCS bas ([Brennan 2018](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/29631516))."
  },
  "next_steps": {
    "advice": "Le score GCS-Pupils n’est pas destiné à remplacer le GCS en tant qu’instantané de l’état d’un patient individuel et de son évolution dans le temps ; les auteurs précisent qu’il vise à servir de complément afin d’ajouter des informations sur la gravité et le pronostic ([Brennan 2018](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/29631516)).",
    "critical_actions": "",
    "management": ""
  },
  "evidence": "",
  "more_info": "| GCS-Pupils Score | Mortality at 6 months post-injury | Unfavorable outcome (vegetative state or severe disability) at 6 months post-injury |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | 74.45% | 89.59% |\n| 2 | 64.62% | 85.22% |\n| 3 | 40.92% | 65.53% |\n| 4 | 39.47% | 68.90% |\n| 5 | 32.57% | 57.75% |\n| 6 | 24.97% | 46.26% |\n| 7 | 19.17% | 37.20% |\n| 8 | 20.04% | 33.55% |\n| 9 | 18.75% | 30.32% |\n| 10 | 17.35% | 28.88% |\n| 11 | 11.60% | 21.81% |\n| 12 | 9.43% | 19.92% |\n| 13 | 7.07% | 15.85% |\n| 14 | 5.64% | 14.39% |\n| 15 | 2.54% | 11.75% |",
  "short_description": "GCS intégrant la réactivité pupillaire.",
  "medium_description": "Combines GCS et pupil reactivity pour greater accuracy at faible GCS.",
